A. Commit message:
fbdev: hyperv_fb: Allow graceful removal of framebuffer

B. Change summary:
The patch moves the release of the framebuffer and associated memory to the fb_ops.fb_destroy function so that the framebuffer framework can handle it gracefully. It also replaces manual registration/unregistration of the framebuffer with devm_register_framebuffer.

C. Compatibility Risk:
Medium

D. Fixed Code:
diff --git a/drivers/video/fbdev/hyperv_fb.c b/drivers/video/fbdev/hyperv_fb.c
index 9798a34ac571..75338ffc703f 100644
--- a/drivers/video/fbdev/hyperv_fb.c
+++ b/drivers/video/fbdev/hyperv_fb.c
@@ -1226,14 +1240,10 @@ static void hvfb_remove(struct hv_device *hdev)
 
 	fb_deferred_io_cleanup(info);
 
-	unregister_framebuffer(info);
 	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&par->dwork);
 
 	vmbus_close(hdev->channel);
 	hv_set_drvdata(hdev, NULL);
-
-	hvfb_putmem(info);
-	framebuffer_release(info);
 }
 
